 HISTORY                                                            26 1451
 -------                                                            26 1451
 1. This library was produced by the Low Energy Interaction         26 1451
    Physics (LEIP) group at North Carolina State University, USA.   26 1451
    The thermal scattering law data for Beryllium Metal was         26 1451
    developed using ab initio lattice dynamics (AILD) [1, 2].       26 1451
    Eleven temperatures are available in this library and extend    26 1451
    into the cryogenic range. The Full Law Analysis Scattering      26 1451
    System Hub (FLASSH) system was used to produce File 7 MT = 2,   26 1451
    4 data for Beryllium [3]. The coherent elastic data were        26 1451
    prepared using the cubic approximation. MAT=26 and ZA=126 are   26 1451
    used for Beryllium Metal. Elemental AWR and free-atom cross     26 1451
    section were computed from MF=3, MT=2 at 1e-5 eV from the ENDF  26 1451
    /B-VIII.0 nuclide evaluation [4].                               26 1451
